\par\par \b \uc2 SNB sight deposits hit highest on record last week\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joshua Franklin   \par \uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2015\par 15:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 ZURICH, April 27 (Reuters) - The amount of cash commercial banks hold with the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  hit the highest on record last week - when the franc marked its biggest fall in two months - suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soared against the euro following the SNB's shock decision in January to scrap a 1.20-per-euro cap on the franc.\par \par \uc2 The safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since pared some gains, and sight deposits data is closely followed for signs of possible SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to weaken the franc, which would support Switzerland's export-driven economy.\par \par \uc2 Sight deposits stood at 385.899 billion francs ($403.4 billion) in the week ending April 24, SNB data showed on Monday, up from 383.984 billion francs the previous week and the highest since public records began in 2004.\par \par \uc2 "The fact the sight deposits rose implies that the SNB has probably been active buying foreign assets, particularly euro-denominated assets," said IG Bank market analyst Andreas Ruhlmann.\par \par \uc2 Sight deposits - which can be freely transferred or converted into cash - measure the amount of money commercial banks hold with the SNB.\par \par \uc2 The SNB can expand such deposits through \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and repurchases of its own debt.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for the SNB declined to comment when asked about possible market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened 0.8 percent against the euro last week, the biggest weekly slide since the middle of February.\par \par \uc2 The SNB's move last week to reduce the number of institutions exempt from negative rates on their cash deposits held at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also put downward pressure on the franc.\par \par \uc2 SNB Chairman \uc2 Thomas Jordan\uc2  stressed again last week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken what it sees as too strong a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, \uc2 Zuercher Kantonalbank\uc2  economist David Marmet said any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the SNB at the moment would probably be on a small scale.\par \par \uc2 "They can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but ... not with a bazooka," Marmet said. "If they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  it's a small \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." ($1 = 0.9566 Swiss francs) (Editing by Susan Fenton) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-4-27T14:32:05.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150427eb4r00eb7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
