\par\par \b \uc2 Will Denmark Throw in the Towel on the Peg?\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tommy Stubbington   \par \uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2015\par 10:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  shocked markets last month by abandoning its cap on the value of the Swiss franc against a plunging euro. Since then, speculation has been rife in markets that \uc2 Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be the next to throw in the towel.\par \par \uc2 With almost alarming regularity, the Nationalbanken, \uc2 Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has lowered interest rates four times already this year to limit the krone's appeal and defend its peg--which is intended to provide a stable backdrop for Danish companies.\par \par \uc2 The peg seeks to stop the euro falling more than 2.25% below (or rising 2.25% above--although that's not the issue right now) 7.46038 krone, by buying (or selling) foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank's also stepped up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and even suspended issuance of government bonds in a bid to lower the krone.\par \par \uc2 But all the rate cutting has fueled talk that the \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is starting to think twice about the huge quantities of foreign assets it needs to buy to defend the peg.\par \par \uc2 Jens Nordvig, head of fixed income research at Nomura, notes that so far this year the Nationalbanken has increased its reserves by more than $30 billion as it buys foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold down the krone. That means in terms of the size of its economy, Denmark is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a similar pace to that of \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  right before the Swiss bank decided to remove the limit on the exchange rate between the franc and the euro.\par \par \uc2 "There is no doubt that the pressure on the krone is very significant, and that the fight for the peg will be a tough one," Nordvig said.\par \par \uc2 But investors shouldn't get carried away with the Swiss-Danish parallels. That's because the background to Denmark's peg is very different, according to Mr. Nordvig.\par \par \uc2 Unlike the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cap, a recent innovation introduced in 2011 to deal with the franc's strength during the euro crisis, the Danish peg has been around since 1982 (when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was pegged to the Deutschmark). And the Danish peg has widespread political support and the backing of all major political parties. There's no sign of the popular opposition to monetary policy that led to a Swiss referendum late last year aiming to force the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold more gold.\par \par \uc2 As long as the political will remains, analysts reckon the Nationalbanken has the tools at its disposal to defend the peg. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  trying to prop up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling reserves (like Russia recently) can run out of assets to sell. But buying assets to weaken your \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is, at least theoretically, a limitless exercise.\par \par \uc2 "Even if a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  turns insolvent for a while, IT IS A \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They don't care about liquidity, and can survive technical insolvency [in the] worst case," said Aurelija Augulyte, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Nordea\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Access Investor Kit for \uc2 Schweizerische Nationalbank\par \par \uc2 Visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=CH0001319265"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=CH0001319265}}}\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 18, 2015 04:11 ET (09:11 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150218eb2i000tl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
