\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Swiss sight deposits rise, add to signs of possible SNB  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2015\par 13:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with strategist comment)\par \par \uc2 ZURICH, Feb 9 (Reuters) - The amount of cash commercial banks hold with the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  crept up slightly last week, adding to signs that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the franc since removing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's cap last month.\par \par \uc2 The SNB on Jan. 15 scrapped the 1.20-per-euro cap it imposed on the Swiss franc in September 2011, surprising financial markets. Maintaining the policy would have cost the bank 100 billion francs ($108 billion) in January alone, the SNB later said.\par \par \uc2 The move sent the safe-haven franc soaring against the euro, though the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has regained some ground amid speculation that the SNB is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.\par \par \uc2 In the week ending Feb. 6, sight deposits rose to 384.889 billion francs, SNB data showed on Monday, from 383.325 billion the previous week.\par \par \uc2 An SNB spokeswoman declined to comment on Monday when asked whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sight deposits - which can be freely transferred or converted into cash - measure the amount of money commercial banks hold with the SNB. The SNB can expand such deposits through \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and repurchases of its own debt.\par \par \uc2 "I think they (the SNB) are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and they haven't tried to pretend that they're not," said \uc2 Jane Foley\uc2 , a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 "But what we saw last week was euro/dollar off its lows, and I think that relieved some of the pressure for the Swiss and the other European central bankers too."\par \par \uc2 SNB Chairman \uc2 Thomas Jordan\uc2  said in an interview broadcast on Saturday that the bank is prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and has room to push interest rates further into negative territory, if necessary, to weaken the franc.\par \par \uc2 Jordan declined to say whether the SNB had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently, though data last week showing \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves hit a record high in January also pointed to \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The SNB has attempted to discourage new flows into francs - viewed as an ultra-safe investment - by imposing an interest rate of -0.75 percent on some cash deposits.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 0.9235 Swiss francs) (Reporting by Alice Baghdjian and Joshua Franklin in Zurich and Jemima Kelly in London; Editing by John Stonestreet and Susan Fenton) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-2-9T13:47:37.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150209eb2900kjl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
