\par\par \b \uc2 Swiss  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves rise sharply in December\b0\par\par\uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2015\par 09:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 ZURICH, Jan 7 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose sharply in December, data showed on Wednesday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month to keep a lid on the red-hot franc.\par \par \uc2 The figures are the first indication of \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month, when a rapidly weakening Russian rouble pushed the franc up further and prompted the SNB to defend a three-year old cap on the franc against the euro by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said last month it would start charging banks for deposits in francs for the first time since the 1970s, hoping to stem a flight to the safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  driven by concern over the euro zone and Russia's deepening crisis.\par \par \uc2 The SNB held 495.104 billion Swiss francs ($490.15 billion) in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of December, compared with 462.669 billion francs in November, revised from an originally reported 462.395 billion, preliminary data calculated according to the standards of the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  showed.\par \par \uc2 The SNB capped the soaring franc in September 2011 to help stave off recession and the threat of deflation and was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in 2012 as the euro zone crisis flared, swelling its already large foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. ($1 = 1.0101 Swiss francs) (Reporting By Katharina Bart and Paul Arnold; Editing by Victoria Bryan) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-1-7T09:16:56.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150107eb17006si\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
