\par\par \b \uc2 Swiss c.bank should use any franc weakness to unwind  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  -IMF\b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2013\par 16:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * SNB could unwind \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions amid franc weakness\par \par \uc2 * IMF report compiled earlier in May, before franc slide\par \par \uc2 ZURICH, May 21 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  should use any weakness in the franc to unwind the large foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves it has built up to keep a lid on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  said in a report released on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The SNB set a cap of 1.20 Swiss francs to the euro in September 2011 to help stave off recession and the threat of deflation.\par \par \uc2 It then \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily last year as the euro zone crisis flared, selling francs and swelling its own foreign reserves to prevent its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening as investors sought safety in the franc.\par \par \uc2 The SNB should maintain its cap on the franc, given low inflation and growth and the risk of further capital inflows, the IMF said in the report, compiled early in May before the franc hit multi-month lows against the dollar and euro.\par \par \uc2 "The authorities should also take full advantage of any capital outflows to unwind past \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the IMF's executive board said in its \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  consultation report, concluded on May 8.\par \par \uc2 The franc hit a nine-month low against the dollar and a four-month low against the euro this month and could fall more in coming months as concerns about a euro zone break-up wane and risks of deflation in Switzerland mount.\par \par \uc2 The SNB should also consider introducing negative interest rates on excess bank reserves if the franc comes under fresh appreciation pressures, the IMF said, reiterating views expressed in a March statement.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still sees the franc as overvalued and will continue to defend its cap as long as necessary, SNB board member Fritz Zurbruegg was quoted as saying last week.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Alice Baghdjian; Editing by Hugh Lawson)\par \par \uc2 EMBARGOED SNB-IMF/ | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130521e95l000nn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
