\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Swiss CPI Data Give SNB Free Reign to  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2012\par 14:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 8:45 EDT - With falling consumer prices in \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can do what it needs to do defend the 1.20 peg against the euro, says \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 . "Deflation is the order of the game, which gives the SNB a free hand to print money if they need to." It adds that with deflation, there's "no reason for them to step back from that floor." The firmer euro this week will take some heat off SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but any more euro-zone tensions could intensify CHF demand and make the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "busy again," warns \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 . The euro is at CHF1.2016, little changed on the day. (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 08:38 EDT - Desjardins Group's Jimmy Jean says the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 's new approach to scheduling policy statements and policy reports will help provide more cohesive messaging from the bank and thus could help reduce volatility. The old approach saw the policy statement released on Tuesday and the quarterly report the day after. The bank announced Friday it will now do both on Wednesdays. Although the precise format has yet to be unveiled, it reduces the possibility of discrepant messages from the statement and the policy, which has occurred under the old system, Jean said. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:34 EDT - Whereas \uc2 Procter & Gamble\uc2  (PG) struggles to sell more products, \uc2 Church & Dwight\uc2  (CHD) is finding little problem boosting sales volume. Its rose 6.3%, though revenue rose less amid "unfavorable product mix and pricing." One thing driving that is CHD is selling more of its lower-priced--and lower-margin--household products like laundry detergent while sales of more-profitable personal-care items like Orajel and battery-operated toothbrushes were weaker. As such, CHD now sees 2012 margins at the low end of prior views. And as the company otherwise backed year targets, the 3Q EPS estimate is below consensus. sis a couple pennies light of estimates. CHD, still inactive premarket, has gained 22% this year. (paul.ziobro@dowjones.com; @pziobro)\par \par \uc2 8:25 EDT - Supply is the main focus. This week's $72bln sales will start at 1 pm EDT with $32 bln in 3-year maturity, followed by $24bln in 10-yr Wednesday and $16 bln in 30-year Thursday. The selling could be a boon for the auction given historically slim yields. The 10-year note is 11/32 lower to yield 1.596%, just about 22bp away from a record low made in June. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:24 EDT - While \uc2 Lowe's\uc2  (LOW) has mixed itself up in a potentially bruising battle to buy Canadian peer Rona (RON.T) in a fight that could ultimately top $2B if LOW lands its prey, \uc2 Home Depot\uc2  (HD) announces a much-more-modest $93M deal for US Home Systems (USHS). The company has exclusively offered products and services like kitchen and bath refacing through the retailer for some time. The deal for USHS comes as its stock more than doubled to start 2012, approaching $15, before pulling back the $8-10 range the past 4 months. HD has agreed to pay $12.50. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 08:19 ET - Risk appetite is a little bit firmer as seen in the lift in EUR/USD and global equities, says \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 's Jane Foley. But with relatively quiet markets, she notes that the boost still stems from residual optimism from US payrolls and hopes that the ECB will do something to support Italian and Spanish bonds next month. She says for now, the slow event calendar will likely leave EUR/USD rangebound: "We're still waiting for the next happening from the eurozone." The improved market tone is also pushing the classic safe haven yen lower. EUR/USD up 0.2% at 1.2431, while USD/JPY advances 0.3% to a session high at 78.48. (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:15 EDT - Tudor Pickering says the big fire at \uc2 Chevron\uc2 's (CVX) Richmond, Calif., refinery should help Tesoro (TSO), which has most of its assets on the West Coast. CVX's facility accounts for nearly 10% of the region's fuel-refining capacity, and so far it's unclear whether it will be out for a prolonged period. TSO, already a darling of investors with its 40% stock jump this year, is inactive premarket while CVX is down 0.3% in light activity. (angel.gonzalez@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:10 EDT - While HCA's solid 2Q results got lost Monday among the worries about a federal inquiry and what the New York Times might say about the hospital operator, rival Tenet (THC) comes in with its own strength as both the top and bottom lines surprisingly grew. While total admissions edged lower, surgeries and emergency-room visits each climbed some 5%. On an adjusted basis, admissions rose for a 7th-straight quarter. The news should be solace for a stock that's been down 23% the past 6 months after a strong post-Thanksgiving rally. THC, inactive premarket, is down 9.2% this year. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:09 EDT - \uc2 Hewlett-Packard\uc2  (HPQ) chief \uc2 Meg Whitman\uc2 's "smart moves" aren't enough to keep \uc2 UBS\uc2  from starting the challenged computing giant at sell, citing a "lack of focus" between corporate and consumer businesses. Bank suggests HPQ might be better off spinning out its PC business, an option Whitman rejected last year, as well as its printer unit, which faces broader revenue pressure. HPQ off 1% at $18.50 premarket. (andrew.fitzgerald@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:05 EDT - The Canadian dollar is modestly firmer and is holding the US dollar below the dollar-for-dollar, even-Steven level as the backdrop for the commodity- and equity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears supportive. But relatively robust support for the greenback below parity is likely to make further moves hard-fought for the loonie. Importantly, the US dollar has not closed below parity since May 8. It was trading recently at C$0.9981, versus C$1.0003 late Monday, according to CQG. (karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:02 EDT - Investors are sure to like Sirius XM's (SIRI) improved 2Q revenue and soaring profit on tax benefits, but expect more focus today on SIRI's feud with John Malone for control of the company. The 2Q earnings call should give SIRI's brash CEO \uc2 Mel Karmazin\uc2  a chance to rebut Malone's quip last month that he's only focused on the company's short-term health. Investors will also look for any updates on how the FCC views Liberty Media's (LMCA) efforts to take over the satellite operator. SIRI trades 2.3% higher premarket at $2.27. (william.launder@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:01 EDT - \uc2 Health Net\uc2  (HNT) shares have tumbled 21% since the health insurer's latest negative report and guidance cut, on Friday, but BMO Capital Markets is bracing for more bad news. Firm downgrades HNT to underperform from market perform "reflecting our concerns around the company's structure and strategy." On the commercial front, HNT "lacks the scale" to serve sicker patients who choose the company's full-network insurance product over different offerings that have thinner benefits, BMO says. And in Medicaid, California's constant budget pressure has long made that program a challenge. "We believe there is more downside to come," BMO says. (jon.kamp@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Market Talk Editors, \par Bradley Davis, 212 416-2654, bradley.davis@dowjones.com \par Kevin Kingsbury, 212 416-2354, kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Patrick Sullivan, 212 416-2326,Patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 08-07-12 0845ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120807e8870007g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
