\par\par \b \uc2 Sov. wealth fund wouldn't help cap franc-Jordan\b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2012\par 10:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 ZURICH, June 14 (Reuters) - The chairman of the Swiss National Bank on Thursday rejected the idea of using foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to create a sovereign wealth fund, saying it would not help defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's cap of 1.20 per euro on the safe-haven Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 "The creation of such a fund would not help to enforce the minimum exchange rate," Chairman Thomas Jordan said in the text of a speech for the bank's quarterly policy review. "It does little to assist Switzerland or Swiss monetary policy."\par \par \uc2 The SNB's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings have risen sharply in recent years as the bank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the franc's rise during the euro zone's debt crisis. The SNB capped the franc at 1.20 per euro last Sept. 6, threatening unlimited \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed.\par \par \uc2 Some politicians and commentators in \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  have suggested the SNB create a sovereign wealth fund to help boost the return on its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings, which are now chiefly invested in highly rated government debt.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Catherine Bosley and Katharina Bart)\par \par \uc2 SWISS-SNB/FUND (URGENT) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120617e86e0002q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
