\par\par \b \uc2 "Country Forecast Switzerland September 2011" added to ReportBuyer.com\b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2011\par \uc2 M2 Presswire\par \uc2 MTPW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011, M2 Communications. All rights reserved.   \par \par \uc2 New report: Country Forecast Switzerland September 2011:\par \par \uc2 ReportBuyer.com has added a new report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.reportbuyer.com/go/EIU04288"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.reportbuyer.com/go/EIU04288}}}\par \par \uc2 Summary of Report -\par \par \uc2 Overview\par \par \uc2 Switzerland faces risks to financial and economic stability from the stark appreciation of the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and from the worsening of the euro area debt crisis. The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  (SNB, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will attempt to peg the franc\u8217\'20\'19s exchange rate to the euro, but there is a risk that it will fail. In terms of the euro crisis, Switzerland is hostage to the attempts of European policymakers to solve a systemic crisis. A euro break-up remains possible and would be extremely negative for the Swiss economy. After the October 2011 general election, the coalition of the four largest parties is expected to be renewed. The Swiss People\u8217\'20\'19s Party (SVP) will remain the largest party and is set to regain a second seat in the seven-person government. The policy agenda will continue to focus on improving the business environment, restraining healthcare cost growth and reforming social security systems. Bilateral engagement with the EU will continue, but could become more difficult. The general government budget balance is expected to record small deficits during 2011-13 and return to surplus in 2015. The Economist Intelligence Unit believes that GDP growth will slow to average around 1.6% a year in 2011-15. We expect inflation to remain low throughout 2011-15, at an average of about 1%. The current-account surplus is forecast to fall to around 6% of GDP by 2015.\par \par \uc2 Key changes from last month\par \par \uc2 Political outlook\par \par \uc2 The resignation of the Swiss minister of foreign affairs, Micheline Calmy-Rey, is not likely to change the distribution of government seats after the general election.\par \par \uc2 Economic policy outlook\par \par \uc2 The SNB\u8217\'20\'19s decision to peg the Swiss franc to the euro in September 2011 represents a dramatic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There is a good chance that it will be able to enforce the peg, but the move does bring some medium-term risks to price stability.\par \par \uc2 Economic forecast\par \par \uc2 We have adjusted our exchange rate forecast to around Swfr1.20:\u226\'00\'E2\u8218\'20\'1A\u172\'00\'AC1 for 2011-13, to reflect the impact of the SNB\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Country Forecast \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  September 2011: , is available at:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.reportbuyer.com/countries/europe/switzerland/country_forecast_switzerland_september_2011.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.reportbuyer.com/countries/europe/switzerland/country_forecast_switzerland_september_2011.html}}}\par \par \uc2 M2 Communications disclaims all liability for information provided within M2 PressWIRE. Data supplied by named party/parties. Further information on M2 PressWIRE can be obtained at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.presswire.net"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.presswire.net}}}\uc2  on the world wide web. Inquiries to info@m2.com.\par \par \uc2 Dokument MTPW000020111004e7a4004h8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
