\par\par \b \uc2 Norway c.bank chief says could react quickly\b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2011\par 10:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  OSLO, Sept 8 (Reuters) - Norway's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Thursday the bank could react quickly to changes in the economic outlook after the Nordic country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened due to \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2  "A too strong crown could over time lead to too low inflation and too low growth", \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Oeystein Olsen said in a speech published on \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2 's website.\par \par \uc2  "That would in that case be addressed by taking action through monetary policy," he said, adding that setting the deposit rate would be the tool in question.\par \par \uc2   Olsen on Wednesday admitted the strong crown would have an impact on policy, but stressed he was in no danger of following \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken it. \par \par \uc2  "Monetary policy can react quickly to changes in the economic outlook," he said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2   The crown weakened on Thursday and traded at 7.5748 against the euro at 0818 GMT after surging to new eight-year highs below 7.49 on the two preceding days.  \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Oslo newsroom)\par \par \uc2 NORWAY-CBANK/ (URGENT)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110908e798000ir\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
