\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Model-driven hedge funds among losers in SNB shock\b0\par\par\uc2 986 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2011\par 18:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Concepts was short CHF pre-SNB, but loses on options\par \par \uc2 * Many CTAs, macro funds long Swiss franc, likely hit\par \par \uc2 * Some funds went short the franc before \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move\par \par \uc2 * Swiss fund of funds came out ahead\par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Concepts' Taylor comments, details)\par \par \uc2 By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss and Laurence Fletcher\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK/LONDON, Sept 6 (Reuters) - Hedge funds, betting on global markets and driven by computer models, were among those hardest hit by \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's shock \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday to reverse profitable bets on the Swiss franc's "safe-haven" status.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  surprised investors with an exchange rate cap, saying it would no longer tolerate a rate below 1.20 francs per euro and would defend the target by buying other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in unlimited quantities. For details, see [ID:nL5E7K61FL]\par \par \uc2 The news sent the franc tumbling nearly 10 percent against the euro <EURCHF=EBS> on trading platform EBS. In late trading, the euro was still up 8.7 percent against the franc on the day to change hands at 1.2047.\par \par \uc2 John Taylor, chairman and chief investment officer of the $8 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedge fund \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Concepts in New York, was able to get the direction right as his fund sold the Swiss franc last week. But he was hit by the sharp drop in the euro/Swiss franc volatility in the options market.\par \par \uc2 "We made money on the outrights because we were short Swiss francs, but because vols were so high, we were happily pocketing the premium for a while and that cost us a bunch of money today because volatility dropped," Taylor said.\par \par \uc2 "So net-net, our fund is down," Taylor added.\par \par \uc2 One-month implied volatilities -- a measure of the market's view of the extent of future \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements -- in the euro/Swiss franc dropped to 9.95 percent on Tuesday from 22 percent on Monday. Vols hit a record high of around 30 percent in early August.\par \par \uc2 Overall, the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Concepts chairman thinks 1.20 francs is a feasible entry level to buy the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the euro, especially if the euro zone's sovereign debt situation worsens.\par \par \uc2 Managed futures funds, which latch onto market trends and which have been among the few winning hedge funds strategies in a tough 2011, had hopped on board the franc's appreciation from more than 1.32 per euro in April to just above parity last month. [ID:nL5E7JO2LY]\par \par \uc2 "Obviously, any directional fund will be down today," said Axel Merk, who manages the $750 million \uc2 Merk Hard \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund\uc2  in Palo Alto, California.\par \par \uc2 Merk lost after the SNB move since he had a 1.5 percent exposure on the Swiss franc in his portfolio, but he said he managed to offset those losses by buying the Norwegian crown. In fact, Merk said he bought more crowns last Friday.\par \par \uc2 The Norwegian crown gained 1.2 percent against the euro <EURNOK=> on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The SNB move notwithstanding, Merk said he will still buy the Swiss franc, although it may be too early to purchase it right now since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has obvious political backing to implement its target.\par \par \uc2 "But at some point, I will definitely buy it again since the SNB has made the Swiss franc cheaper," he said.\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MACRO FUNDS' PAIN\par \par \uc2 Some macro funds -- a strategy made famous by the likes of billionaire investor George Soros -- may have suffered after profiting this year from bets that the Swiss franc and Australian dollar will rise.\par \par \uc2 "I'm sure it will hurt," said one fund of hedge funds manager who spoke on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 "It's a massive move. It doesn't have to be that big (a position in a fund) to be painful ... CTAs are highly likely to be hit by that." Commodity trading advisors, or CTAs, is another term for managed futures funds.\par \par \uc2 Among computer funds that may have been hit is Man Group's flagship $23.9 billion AHL fund. An AHL fund manager told Bloomberg Television last month it had a small bet on the franc.\par \par \uc2 Winton Capital, which manages $22.4 billion in assets and whose main fund is up nearly 8 percent so far this year, declined to comment on specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements.\par \par \uc2 Man Group and Bluecrest also declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 One computer-driven fund manager, who was short the euro against the franc as the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  announced it was setting a minimum exchange rate target, said his fund has closed out all its positions in the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 "As it was a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move, we decided to square our positions and now have no market exposure to the Swiss franc," he said. "We have squared our position in the Swiss franc for the future because we will not be able to capture that risk in the quantitative models."\par \par \uc2 Other funds profited from the SNB move. Quaesta Capital, a $3-billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund of funds in Zurich, Switzerland, said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  managers it oversees have gone short Swiss franc this week, posting the biggest outflow as well.\par \par \uc2 In an earlier interview, Pablo Frei, portfolio manager and senior market analyst at Quaesta, said their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  managers have become concerned about the Swiss franc's overvaluation against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Aviva Investors went long the New Zealand dollar versus the Swiss franc in the past few weeks and has seen an 18 percent move. It has also gone long in the Norwegian crown against the franc. [ID:nL5E7K61UO]\par \par \uc2 Hardeep Dogra, \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Manager at Schroder Investment Management in London, said they had been neutral on the franc.\par \par \uc2 It was "precisely because of this quandary," Dogra said. As "much as you like the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , valuation is a problem and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been making repeated comments about its position, that it was aiming for some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness."\par \par \uc2 HEDGEFUNDS/SWISSFRANC (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110906e796000v2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
