\par\par \b \uc2 SNB: Swiss July  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Reserves Drop To CHF182.08 Billion\b0\par\par\uc2 197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 11:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The value of the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves slipped to 182.08 billion Swiss francs ($234.8 billion), \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The value of its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings fell from an unrevised CHF196.3 billion in June, according to data posted on the SNB's website.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly from March 2009 through June 2010 as it sought to check the franc's excessive gains against the euro to head off the danger of deflation.\par \par \uc2 The SNB last month reported a first-half consolidated loss of CHF10.8 billion, with "losses on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions amounting to CHF9.9 billion due to exchange-related valuation losses of around CHF11.7 billion".\par \par \uc2 The book-loss followed franc gains of about 2.5% against the euro and almost 11% against the dollar during the first half of the year as investors sought shelter from the debt crises in the euro zone and the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Website: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.snb.ch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.snb.ch}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Neil MacLucas, Dow Jones Newswires, +41 43 443 8046;\par \par \uc2 neil.mclucas@dowjones.com [ 04-08-11 0941GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110804e784000xv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
