\par\par \b \uc2 DJ FOCUS:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Traders Still Skeptical As SNB Ups Pressure On Japan\b0\par\par\uc2 548 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2011\par 18:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Trader eyes turn to Japan following SNB move to tame Swiss franc\par \par \uc2 --Like the Swiss franc, yen has been strengthening due to its safe-haven status\par \par \uc2 --Japanese authorities seen struggling to tame yen \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Clare Connaghan \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader eyes are turning to Japan and to whether the monetary authorities there will follow the lead taken by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  Wednesday by also acting to counter strength in their country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yet despite widespread expectations for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in support of the yen and for more monetary easing by the Bank of Japan, skepticism abounds in London--easily the world's biggest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market--that any such action will succeed in turning the tide of yen strength.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Like the Swiss franc, the yen has appreciated significantly of late, moving on Monday to within a whisker of its all-time high against the dollar as concerns over global economic growth and the euro-zone debt crisis sent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  investors scrambling for the relative safety of the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 To date, Japan's monetary authorities have done little except crank up the verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rhetoric. But now \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Switzerland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has broken ranks and introduced measures to stem the relentless appreciation of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , pressure on Japan to do something is building.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Rhetoric only has a short shelf-life and they [Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Bank of Japan] know that," said Neil Mellor, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Bank of New York Mellon.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After fretting for months over the relentless appreciation in the Swiss franc, the SNB finally ran out of patience Wednesday and said it will trim its key three-month London Interbank Offered Rate target to as close to zero as possible. The bank said it will also increase the supply of liquidity to the Swiss franc money market by expanding banks' on-call cash deposits.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Such measures raise the stakes for Japan but are still unlikely to spur them into action any time soon, London market participants said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Its very unlikely we're going to get \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Jane Foley a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is also difficult to know which additional measures they could introduce, because there is already so much liquidity in Japan anyway, Foley said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nonetheless, Japan's export community is hopeful of some kind of remedial action soon, with all eyes on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as it prepares to start a two-day policy meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If it is prompted by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly to suppress the yen, now could be the time to do it as thin summer liquidity conditions could result in a bigger immediate market reaction.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But, ultimately, unless sentiment towards global economic growth improves sharply, any measures introduced are seen by traders in London as likely to have a limited impact.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1635 GMT, the dollar was trading at Y76.860 against the yen, compared with Y77.14 in New York Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Clare Connaghan, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 (0) 20 7842 9496; clare.connaghan@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Jessica Mead in London contributed to this article.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 03, 2011 12:48 ET (16:48 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110803e783005l6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
