\par\par \b \uc2 Swiss right-winger wants SNB's powers crimped-paper\b0\par\par\uc2 668 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2011\par 11:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Blocher wants SNB only to focus on price stability\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Swatch Group\uc2  CEO urged more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 ZURICH, July 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's right-wing former justice minister launched a fresh attack on \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  chairman \uc2 Philipp Hildebrand\uc2  in a Sunday newspaper interview and urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to focus exclusively on its task of maintaining price stability.\par \par \uc2 The SNB on Friday reported a 9.9 billion franc loss on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings for the first half of the year due to the surging franc. That follows a hit of 26.5 billion francs last year that led to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reporting its biggest annual loss.\par \par \uc2 National elections are schedule for Oct. 23\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Der Sonntag, Christoph Blocher, mastermind of the right-wing Swiss People's Party (SVP), stepped up the rhetoric against Hildebrand, having earlier this year called on him to resign.\par \par \uc2 "It's untenable. He's been elected by the government -- it should now act," the paper quoted him as saying. "Hildebrand behaves like a speculator and is therefore not qualified for this job."\par \par \uc2 The SNB accumulated vast foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings between March 2009 and June 2010 because it stepped into markets to cap the franc's rise and stave off the risk of deflation.\par \par \uc2 Blocher said the SNB should not be allowed to expand its balance sheet to such an extent without government approval.\par \par \uc2 "The job of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is money supply and price stability -- here it should be independent. It should not be totally independent when it doesn't involve its main objective."\par \par \uc2 Hildebrand, whose term runs until 2015, became the subject of political sparring earlier this year, in part because Switzerland's 26 cantons (states) may not get their customary dividend from the SNB this year, pressuring their budgets.\par \par \uc2 Blocher's proposal would require a change to the Swiss constitution, which enshrines an independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  whose mandate is to ensure price stability.\par \par \uc2 The populist SVP, which in 2009 spearheaded a vote to ban the construction of new minarets, looks set to hang on to its lead as the biggest party in parliament's lower house.\par \par \uc2 MORE \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 While Blocher has said he wants to clip the winsgs of the SNB, the Social Democrats (SP), the second-biggest party in parliament's lower house, have called for more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The safe-haven Swiss franc has risen some 14 percent against the dollar and 7 percent against the euro since the start of the year, drawing complaints from exporters.\par \par \uc2 Forward-looking indicators such as the KOF barometer have pointed to a slowdown in momentum.\par \par \uc2 One of the companies which has been most outspoken about the impact of the strong franc has been \uc2 Swatch Group\uc2  , famous for its colourful plastic timepieces, which has said its turnover target for the year may be a challenge due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an interview with the SonntagsZeitung, Chief Executive \uc2 Nick Hayek\uc2  said many of the problems due to the rampant franc had not yet become evident, that the SNB would simply have to endure the criticism, and that a new round of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  was warranted.\par \par \uc2 "The SNB didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  long enough. The SNB should now signal to the markets that it will not accept a further appreciation without action, and will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 The SNB has said it still has the means to act if deflationary risks were to resurface.\par \par \uc2 "(Hildebrand) should not allow the criticism -- from the politicians, the cantons or the journalists -- to intimidate him," Hayek said.\par \par \uc2 "The national bank must set an exchange rate goal of 1.35 and defend it. That would finally be a clear signal," he also said, and re-stated that in a few years \uc2 Swatch Group\uc2  would achieve 10 billion francs in annual revenue through organic growth.\par \par \uc2 The franc is currently trading at around 1.13 per euro\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Catherine Bosley; Editing by David Cowell)\par \par \uc2 SWISS-SNB/POLITICS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110803e77v000m1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
