\par\par \b \uc2 SNB: To Keep Using Suited, Necessary Instruments To Fulfill Mandate\b0\par\par\uc2 540 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2011\par 19:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--\uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  President \uc2 Philipp Hildebrand\uc2  signalled Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to keep its options open in pursuing its mandate to ensure price stability.\par \par \uc2 Hildebrand also backed the institution's right to act independently, in prepared remarks to a business audience.\par \par \uc2 "We are continually analyzing developments and constantly drawing conclusions with a view to our future actions. Based on this, the SNB will continue to use the instruments we judge best suited and necessary for fulfilling our mandate in the interests of the country as a whole, to the best of our ability," he said.\par \par \uc2 While not detailing specific options open to the SNB, Hildebrand started his speech by mentioning the 21 billion Swiss franc ($25 billion) loss the SNB posted in 2010, when it spent billions of francs attempting to curb the Swiss franc's surge against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the US dollar and euro.\par \par \uc2 Hildebrand said the SNB, which generally pays profits out to the Swiss federation and its cantons, may suspend those payments as it repairs its swollen balance sheet--a result of past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Very volatile results may be expected in the next few years because of the current size of the balance sheet and the uncertain situation in the capital markets," Hildebrand said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had already flagged possible future losses in January 2011, when it disclosed its 2010 loss.\par \par \uc2 Hildebrand also issued a passionate defense of the SNB's independence, which right-wing politicians have argued in favor of clipping.\par \par \uc2 Hildebrand said the SNB's independence is "particularly valuable" in Switzerland because monetary, and not fiscal, policy was mainly used during the financial crisis to stimulate the alpine nation's economy.\par \par \uc2 He also emphasized that the SNB's flexibility in deciding on instruments of monetary policy proved to be a "huge advantage" during the crisis, such as when it issued SNB bills to soak up excess money-market liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss government has repeatedly spoken out in favor of the SNB's independence when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under attack from the Swiss People's Party, or SVP--\b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's largest party--for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the franc.\par \par \uc2 Hildebrand's remarks are noteworthy because he appears not to explicitly rule out more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 --something most economists see as unlikely--and because the remarks are among his most political yet in quieting his detractors, and asserting the SNB's independence.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the SNB delayed curbing its expansive monetary policy, citing the recent surge in the franc as adding to the risks facing the Swiss economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the target range for its benchmark three-month Swiss franc London interbank offered rate on hold at 0.0%-0.75%.\par \par \uc2 The SNB is targeting a three-month Libor rate of 0.25%, a record low in place since March 2009.\par \par \uc2 The strong franc appears to have been a major factor in the SNB's decision to keep rates on hold for at least another quarter, in an effort to avoid lifting rates earlier than the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -By Katharina Bart, Dow Jones Newswires; +41 43 443 8043; katharina.bart@dowjones.com [ 21-06-11 1700GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110621e76l0014y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
