\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Swiss franc hits record highs vs struggling euro\b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 2011\par 10:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Swiss franc soars to record high vs euro\par \par \uc2 * Brushes off SNB comments about strong franc and growth\par \par \uc2 * Traders expect euro/Swiss franc to extend losses\par \par \uc2 LONDON, June 16 (Reuters) - The Swiss franc hit a record high against the euro on Thursday, shrugging off \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns about franc strength and buoyed by demand for the safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to growing concerns about euro zone debt.\par \par \uc2 The euro <EURCHF=> fell more than one percent on the day to hit a record low of 1.1957 francs on trading platform EBS, with traders saying losses had accelerated as stop loss orders were triggered on the break below 1.1970 francs.\par \par \uc2 It failed to break lower, however, with traders saying there were bids at 1.1950 francs.\par \par \uc2 "It feels like momentum in euro/Swiss franc is accelerating to the downside," said Kathleen Brooks, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 .com.\par \par \uc2 Implied volatility in euro/Swiss franc spiked higher, reflecting a perceived risk in the options market of further weakness in the euro/Swiss franc spot price.\par \par \uc2 One-month euro/Swiss implied volatility <EURCHF1MO=> traded above 12.0 percent, up from around 11.2 percent on Wednesday. One-month risk reversals <EUCH1MRR=ICAP> revealed an increasing demand for bets on euro losses versus the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  left interest rates unchanged, stressing risks to the economy from a strong franc, with Chairman \uc2 Philipp Hildebrand\uc2  expressing concerns about exporters' margins. [ID:nLDE75E1S8] [ID:nWEA6270]\par \par \uc2 But analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked unlikely given that \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not facing deflation, adding that authorities would have a battle to prevent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength with risk aversion sparking demand for francs and weighing on the euro.\par \par \uc2 "It doesn't look like the SNB will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and if they did they would be trampled on in the current risk-averse environment," Brooks added.\par \par \uc2 SNB board member \uc2 Jean-Pierre Danthine\uc2  said the Swiss economy was doing well enough that there was no reason at the moment for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  or extraordinary measures. [ID:nWEA6294]\par \par \uc2 Between March 2009 and June 2010 the SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stave off deflationary risks.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc also gained against the dollar, which was down 0.5 percent at 0.8491 francs <CHF=>.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Jessica Mortimer; Editing by Catherine Evans)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /SWISSIE (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110619e76g00085\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
