\par\par \b \uc2 SNB: Swiss  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Reserves Slip To CHF193.8 Billion\b0\par\par\uc2 173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2011\par 09:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The value of the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves slipped to 193.8 billion Swiss francs ($232.3 billion) in May, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The value of the reserves fell CHF8.3 billion from a revised CHF202.1 billion in April, according to the SNB.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly from March 2009 through June 2010 as it sought to check the franc's excessive gains against the euro to head off the danger of deflation.\par \par \uc2 The SNB posted a CHF1.9 billion profit in the first quarter, after a CHF19.2 billion book loss last year, as the euro gained around 3% versus the franc in the three months through March, boosting the value of its euro holdings.\par \par \uc2 At 0704 GMT, the Swiss franc was quoted at CHF1.2224 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Website: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.snb.ch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.snb.ch}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Neil MacLucas, Dow Jones Newswires, +41 43 443 8046; neil.mclucas@dowjones.com [ 06-06-11 0713GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110606e766000d4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
