\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ SNB: Debate On '10 Loss Ignore Swiss Econ In Good Shape\b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 11:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 06:49 EDT *DJ  SNB's Hildebrand: Risks Still Remain For Swiss Economy\par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 07:01 EDT *DJ  Hildebrand Defends SNB's Past \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency Interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 07:03 EDT *DJ  Hildebrand: SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Verdict Only Possible In Few Yrs\par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 07:11 EDT *DJ  SNB Hildebrand: Swiss Exports Resilient, Strong At Moment\par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 07:12 EDT *DJ  SNB's Hildebrand: Franc Already Affecting Swiss Exporters\par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 07:17 EDT DJ  Hildebrand: Debate On SNB's 2010 Loss Ignores State Of Economy\par \par \uc2 GENEVA (Dow Jones)--\uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  President Philipp Hildebrand Tuesday said the public debate over its 2010 loss incurred from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  ignored the fact that the Swiss economy is in good shape.\par \par \uc2 Still, risks to Swiss economic growth remain, Hildebrand told reporters Tuesday at a media briefing in Geneva, \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly between March 2009 and mid-June last year to try to check the appreciation of the franc against the euro.\par \par \uc2 In the process it amassed large reserves of euro, which then depreciated, leaving the SNB with a book loss of 19.2 billion Swiss francs ($21.3 billion) last year, triggering public criticism of the euro purchases.\par \par \uc2 Hildebrand defended the SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and said a final verdict on their success can only be made in a few years' time.\par \par \uc2 -By Goran Mijuk, Dow Jones Newswires; +41 43 443 8047, goran.mijuk@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 07:26 EDT *DJ  SNB's Hildebrand: We Still Face Important Risks\par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 07:27 EDT *DJ  SNB's Hildebrand: Risks Are EU Debt, Middle East and Japan\par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 07:28 EDT *DJ  SNB's Hildebrand: Strong Franc Helped Reduce Swiss Inflation\par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 07:29 EDT *DJ  SNB: Nuclear Aspect Of Japan Disaster Adds To Uncertainty\par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 07:33 EDT *DJ  Hildebrand: SNB Independence Has Great Value, Helped Switzerland\par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 07:36 EDT *DJ  Hildebrand: SNB To Do Everything To Safeguard Price Stability\par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 07:37 EDT *DJ  Hildebrand: SNB Confident On Too-Big-To-Fail Rule Backing\par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 07:58 EDT *DJ  SNB's Hildebrand Ends Press Briefing\par \par \uc2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 22, 2011 07:58 ET (11:58 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110322e73m0025i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
