\par\par \b \uc2 Swiss SVP seeks cap on SNB autonomy after losses\b0\par\par\uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 12:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * SVP to propose new rules in parliament next week\par \par \uc2 * Blocher already called for SNB head to quit\par \par \uc2 * Other parties accuse SVP of electioneering\par \par \uc2 ZURICH, March 6 (Reuters) - The popular right-wing Swiss People's Party (SVP) wants to limit the autonomy of the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  (SNB) on decisions outside its core mandate of price stability after big losses on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If the SNB leaves its actual mission with large \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys, one must be able to supervise the SNB bosses and if necessary stop them," Christoph Blocher, former justice minister and SVP mastermind, told the SonntagsZeitung newspaper.\par \par \uc2 Blocher has already called on SNB chief \uc2 Philipp Hildebrand\uc2  to resign after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted a 2010 loss of 19.2 billion Swiss francs ($20.74 billion) after ill-fated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to fight the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. [ID:nLDE71O14P]\par \par \uc2 The SVP, expected to remain Switzerland's biggest party in national elections in October, plans a motion proposing new rules in parliament next week to control the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "In extreme cases, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys can be necessary to secure price stability. That is why we need disciplinary supervisory rules to prevent the managing board contravening their core mandate and taking on unbelievable risks," Blocher said.\par \par \uc2 The SNB has repeatedly defended the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as being necessary to fight deflation risk from the soaring franc.\par \par \uc2 Blocher also accused Hildebrand of being too much in favour of more integration with the European Union.\par \par \uc2 "I have the suspicion that Mr Hildebrand wants to play a role at the European or even global level. He pleads for opening and integration which does not belong to his area of competency. He also doesn't rule out tying the franc to the euro," he said.\par \par \uc2 However, the other main parties in the coalition government that rules \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  have defended the SNB's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence.\par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Johann Schneider-Ammann said in an interview with the Finanz und Wirtschaft newspaper on Saturday that the SNB had managed to dampen the franc's rise somewhat and said the situation had improved in the meantime.\par \par \uc2 Otto Ineichen from the liberal Free Democrats told the Sonntag newspaper the SVP was going too far with its election campaign and was defaming the SNB with "false accusations".\par \par \uc2 The safe-haven franc has soared to record highs against the euro and the dollar due to unrest in north Africa and the euro zone's debt crisis, prompting calls for the government to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as Swiss exporters suffer.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss government has announced measures to help firms to deal with the strong Swiss franc, including increased funding for the tourism industry and support for companies to boost innovation. [ID:nLDE71F1FO]\par \par \uc2 ($1=.9255 Swiss Franc)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Emma Thomasson; Editing by Jon Loades-Carter)\par \par \uc2 SWISS-SNB/   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110306e7360007d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
