\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: Swiss January  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Reserves Climb To CHF207.9B\b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2011\par 10:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, background and comment.)\par \par \uc2 By Neil MacLucas\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The value of the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves increased to 207.9 billion Swiss francs ($219.6 billion) in January reflecting the euro's rally last month.\par \par \uc2 The value of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings rose CHF5.3 billion from an unrevised CHF202.6 billion in December, according to the SNB data. The euro appreciated by around 4% against the Swiss franc during the same period, boosting the value of those reserves.\par \par \uc2 "The higher reserve valuation is simply due to the slight rally we saw in the euro last month, pushing up the value of those common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings," said Ursina Kubli, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 Bank Sarasin & Cie\uc2 . "It certainly doesn't suggest the SNB conducted any fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases," she added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly from March 2009 to try and stem the franc's excessive gains against the euro, though it appeared to step back from this policy in June last year, saying signs of deflation had disappeared.\par \par \uc2 The SNB is expecting to post a hefty CHF21 billion book loss for last year as the franc's 16% appreciation against the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eroded the value of its euro holdings.\par \par \uc2 The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data also show there was little diversification of its reserves in the final quarter of 2010, with its euro holdings slightly lower at EUR90 billion by the end of the year, and its dollar reserves little changed at $54.3 billion. The value of the SNB's Japanese yen holdings rose marginally to Y1.8 billion.\par \par \uc2 "I'm sure the SNB will diversify its reserves in coming months, taking advantage of any further euro gains to reduce its exposure to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Kubli said.\par \par \uc2 The SNB's euro reserves climbed to EUR90 billion last year, from EUR37 billion at the end of 2009, while the dollar holdings increased to $54.3 billion from $27.6 billion.\par \par \uc2 At 0900 GMT, the Swiss franc was quoted at CHF1.2909 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Website: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.snb.ch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.snb.ch}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Neil MacLucas, Dow Jones Newswires; +41 43 443 8046;\par \par \uc2 neil.mclucas@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 04, 2011 04:14 ET (09:14 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110204e724001mz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
