\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Swiss Franc Continues Its Surge Vs Euro, Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Min Zeng   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2010\par 18:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The Swiss franc rose broadly Wednesday, hitting a record high against the euro as investors continued to seek safety from the euro zone's sovereign-debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved as high as CHF1.2440 versus the euro, extending its rally this week. The franc also strengthened against the dollar to the highest levels since October when it touched the all-time peak against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The Swiss franc benefits from both safe-haven flows driven by the debt problems in the euro-zone periphery and the strong Swiss economic outlook," said Gabriel de Kock, North American head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  in New York. "It is a double positive for the franc and I am bullish on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 De Kock said the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 , the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term to stem the rise in the franc. The previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this year has left a huge overhang of liquidity in the economy and the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  doesn't want to further boost the money supply, he said, adding that the Swiss economy had a relatively shallow recession and recovered more rapidly than some other major countries.\par \par \uc2 Steven Englander, head of G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , noted that the franc's strength is due mainly to the euro-zone debt crisis, which means there are still many potential buyers desiring a haven. Englander said it may not be effective for \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying that, even if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  temporarily pushes down the franc, buyers could return to prop it up.\par \par \uc2 Some market participants noted that thinning liquidity near the end of the year exaggerated part of the price swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Many companies and banks have already closed their books for the end of the year and such flows had little to do with the economic fundamental outlooks, they said.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday afternoon, the dollar was CHF0.9519 from CHF0.9563 late Tuesday, according to EBS via CQG. Against the euro, the franc rose about 0.8% to CHF1.2457.\par \par \uc2 The euro-zone debt worries continued to weigh on the euro, with the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening against the dollar and the yen.\par \par \uc2 The onslaught of credit warnings and downgrades of sovereign ratings over the past few days added to worries that borrowing costs in many euro-zone nations would be pushed up further, undermining their economic outlook at a time when governments are putting out fiscal austerity programs to cut budget deficits.\par \par \uc2 "We remain underweight the euro," said Englander.\par \par \uc2 The euro could fall to as low as $1.27 if it breaks below its late November low of $1.2970, said Hidetoshi Yanagihara, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader and strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2  in New York. "Probably the euro might be hit more against the majors--the dollar and the Swiss franc," he said.\par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.3090 from $1.3096 late Tuesday. The dollar was at Y83.57 from Y83.75, while the euro was at Y109.38 from Y109.70.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 80.692 from 80.718.\par \par \uc2 The pound was another big loser, touching a three-month trough against the dollar as a weaker-than-forecast economic report raised worries about the health of the British economy.\par \par \uc2 The U.K. pound was at $1.5380 from $1.5468.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar rose against its U.S. counterpart as a rise in U.S. stocks spurred some investors to buy higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has surged this year, benefiting from strong exports of commodities, thanks to strong demand from China.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar returned to parity against the U.S. dollar for the first time in a week. It rose about 0.27% to $1.0007, near the record peak of $1.0184 hit on November 5.\par \par \uc2 -By Min Zeng, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2096; min.zeng@dowjones.com [ 12-22-10 1236ET ]\par \par \uc2 1074 1863 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101222e6cm000a1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
