\par\par \b \uc2 SNB: Swiss  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Reserves At CHF212.4B By End-November\b0\par\par\uc2 174 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2010\par 09:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The value of the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose slightly to 212.4 billion Swiss francs ($218.2 billion) in November, according to data released Monday.\par \par \uc2 The value of the reserves edged up by CHF500 million from an unrevised CHF211.9 billion in October.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the first half of the year to try to curb the franc's excessive gains against the euro, though it appeared to step back from this policy in June, saying signs of deflation had disappeared.\par \par \uc2 The SNB posted a hefty CHF8.5 billion book loss in the first nine months of the year as the franc's 11% appreciation against the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eroded the value of its euro holdings.\par \par \uc2 At 0809 GMT, the Swiss franc was quoted at 1.3011 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Website: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.snb.ch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.snb.ch}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Neil MacLucas, Dow Jones Newswires, +41 43 443 8046; neil.mclucas@dowjones.com [ 06-12-10 0814GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101206e6c6000ic\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
