\par\par \b \uc2 SNB: Swiss  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Reserves CHF211.9B At End-Oct\b0\par\par\uc2 200 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2010\par 09:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The value of the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves declined to 211.9 billion Swiss francs ($218.5 billion) in October from an unrevised CHF215.3 billion francs at the end of September, according to data released Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The drop of CHF3.4 billion from September signals that the buying of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the franc's appreciation against the euro continued to tail off from the levels seen earlier this year.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the first half of the year to try and curb the franc's excessive gains against the euro, though it appeared to step back from this policy in June, saying signs of deflation had disappeared.\par \par \uc2 The SNB posted a hefty CHF2.8 billion book loss in the first half of the year as the franc's 10% appreciation against the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diminished the value of its euro holdings.\par \par \uc2 At 0711 GMT, the Swiss franc was quoted at 1.3741 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Website: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.snb.ch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.snb.ch}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Neil MacLucas, Dow Jones Newswires, +41 43 443 8046; neil.mclucas@dowjones.com [ 04-11-10 0820GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101104e6b4000ss\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
