\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-SNB says policy appropriate without  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 740 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2010\par 18:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Hildebrand, Danthine: policy right given inflation f'cast\par \par \uc2 * Danthine says no legitimacy for \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  now\par \par \uc2 * Danthine says c.bank may act if shocks lead to deflation\par \par \uc2 (Adds further Hildebrand comment)\par \par \uc2 By Sven Egenter and Silke Koltrowitz\par \par \uc2 LAUSANNE/LUGANO, Switzerland, Oct 28 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's expansionary policy is appropriate and there is no reason at present to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market given the inflation outlook, Swiss central bankers said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at an event in Lausanne, SNB board member \uc2 Jean-Pierre Danthine\uc2  said \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this year to fight a rise in the Swiss franc had been necessary to fend off deflation risks that had now eased. The SNB changed its stance in June.\par \par \uc2 "The current monetary policy is appropriate. In that context we have no legitimacy to go beyond standard monetary policy instruments," Danthine said at a conference, when asked about the SNB's stance on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We are now projecting inflation which is comfortably in positive territory," Danthine said. At the same time, there were no inflationary pressures.\par \par \uc2 But as the Swiss economy was still vulnerable to external shocks and deflationary risks could resurface, the SNB would take the necessary measures, he added.\par \par \uc2 SNB chairman \uc2 Philipp Hildebrand\uc2 , at a separate event in Lugano, said it was important for Switzerland that Europe returned to stability and also issued a warning that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready to take action against house price inflation if necessary, saying it was monitoring the real estate market closely.\par \par \uc2 "The main problem is the lack of confidence in Europe that has shown its effects via turbulence on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that represents a difficult challenge for \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Hildebrand said.\par \par \uc2 The SNB dropped its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in June after spending some 200 billion Swiss francs in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The franc has since hit record highs against the euro and the dollar, though it has softened in recent days <EURCHF=><CHF=>.\par \par \uc2 The SNB indicated at its last policy meeting in September that it was in no rush to lift its target rate for three-month Swiss franc LIBOR from the current ultra-low level of 0.25 percent as it sees a marked slowdown of the economy in 2011.\par \par \uc2 Danthine echoed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's assessment, saying that following a number of strong quarters, the Swiss economy was now set to slow markedly, as the cooling of the global economy and the strength of the Swiss franc were taking their toll.\par \par \uc2 Switzerland emerged from the global downturn less bruised than many other European countries, and the SNB expects growth of around 2.5 percent this year. [ID:nLDE68D1IK]\par \par \uc2 A number of economic data and surveys have recently supported the SNB's view of a slowdown and markets will now closely watch the country's leading growth barometer, the KOF indictor, due on Friday <ECONCH>.\par \par \uc2 HOUSE PRICES\par \par \uc2 Hildebrand also said the SNB's expansionary monetary policy was appropriate, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main focus remained ensuring price stability.\par \par \uc2 ""The SNB will do everything to fulfill its mandate to preserve price stability. We do not want inflation above 2 percent and we do not want deflation," he said.\par \par \uc2 But he also emphasised that the real estate market was being monitored closely. The SNB could take action together with bank regulator FINMA, if necessary, while the SNB was also looking into macro-prudential measures to complement monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 "The longer monetary policy remains expansive, the bigger the risk of undesirable developments. Today some warning signs are already visible," Hildebrand said.\par \par \uc2 Hildebrand's remarks follow a warning from the SNB in June that mortgage lending standards could be too lax.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, SNB Vice Chairman \uc2 Thomas Jordan\uc2  said earlier this year that regulators might consider measures to tackle the real estate market if hiking interest rates was not an option.\par \par \uc2 Low mortgage rates combined with competition among lenders constituted fertile ground for growing risks, Hildebrand said.\par \par \uc2 "Even if the development of real estate prices until now seems to be supported by fundamentals, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its base scenario sees a moderate development in the housing market for the coming year, from the perspective of risk there are indeed grounds for concern," he said. (Additional reporting by Catherine Bosley; Additional writing by Jason Rhodes; Editing by Catherine Evans and Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 SWISS-SNB/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101028e6as00230\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
