\par\par \b \uc2 Swiss firms must live with stong franc - bank lobby\b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 12:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Head of bankers' association says strong franc is to stay\par \par \uc2  * Says Swiss industry needs to adapt quickly\par \par \uc2  * Says systematic \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be challenged by markets\par \par \uc2  ZURICH, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The Swiss industry needs to swiftly adapt to the strong Swiss franc, as its strength will last and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  is limited, the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top banking association said.  "The Swiss franc has always been a problem in Switzerland and today we have a hiccup which could work to the detriment of some (sectors) of our export industry," Patrick Odier, Chairman of the Swiss Bankers' Association, said on Thursday ahead of a key \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  rate-setting meeting.\par \par \uc2  "The question is how swiftly can the Swiss industry adapt to the situation of the strong franc, which will last," he said.\par \par \uc2  Odier noted that some sectors, like exporters, were more at risk from the strength of the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2  Others, such as the wealth management sector, have benefitted as nervous investors moved some of their assets out of the euro zone and into Switzerland.\par \par \uc2  Odier said he did not expect the SNB, whose focus is inflationary or deflationary risks, to look only at specific sectors when taking monetary policy decisions.\par \par \uc2  But he noted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had little room to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to bring down the franc.\par \par \uc2  "The way to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to try and calm down the momentum on the height Swiss franc is limited, but it still exists," he said.\par \par \uc2  "It is my view that whatever a national bank does massively and openly against or for a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be nearly always systematically challenged by the market," he added.\par \par \uc2  "We should not exaggerate (the impact from the Swiss franc). We should watch the impact of the high franc on the industry in general and hope for a quick adaptation of some of these companies that may suffer the most."\par \par \uc2  (Reporting by Lisa Jucca; Editing by Toby Chopra)  \par \par \uc2 SWISS-FRANC/BANKERS|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100916e69g000qn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
