\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ SNB WATCH: Bank Faces Test Of Resolve As Euro Set To Slide\b0\par\par\uc2 By Neil MacLucas  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 724 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2010\par 12:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's claim of further leeway to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets could draw fresh scrutiny in coming days because the euro is expected to weaken to all-time lows versus the Swiss franc, according to analysts.\par \par \uc2 SNB President \uc2 Philipp Hildebrand\uc2  reiterated in a newspaper interview Saturday that preserving price stability remains its main goal, and that should the boundaries for such stability be breached, the bank could certainly act to prevent a further appreciation of the franc.\par \par \uc2 Analysts, though, are skeptical about the strength of the SNB's resolve to re-enter the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after it signaled in June that purchases of euros would be halted because signs of deflation have disappeared.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this year and last was certainly necessary, but I don't think it is something the SNB will want to repeat right now," said Beat Siegenthaler, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS AG.\par \par \uc2 Hildebrand was adamant the SNB's earlier forays into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market were successful damage-limitation exercises, helping prevent a deflationary spiral and an unemployment rate of as much as 8% in \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 One consequence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, was a swelling of the SNB's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to CHF219 billion at the end of July, from around CHF95 billion at the end of 2009, resulting in a book loss of CHF2.8 billion as the value of those euro reserves slid.\par \par \uc2 With fresh concerns about a global economic slowdown resurfacing, and equity markets struggling to hold on to any significant gains, investors are increasingly likely to try to avoid risk by opting for the relative safety of the franc.\par \par \uc2 "Aversion to risky investments is raising its head again, and we are looking for the market to at least test the recent all-time low in EUR/CHF of 1.3072 in coming days," said \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analyst Antje Praefcke.\par \par \uc2 The euro managed to rally to just short of the CHF1.40 level earlier in August, but fears about slowing economic growth in the U.S. and Japan have put the skids under the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  once more.\par \par \uc2 The euro was at CHF1.3142 by 0815 GMT, with technical analysts expecting a test of the 1.3072 level this week, and then the key 1.3000 mark.\par \par \uc2 UBS\uc2  is doubtful the SNB will want to show its hand in the market right now because this tends to focus the spotlight on the franc, and attracts global speculative flows.\par \par \uc2 "Any SNB activity just stirs interest from the hedge funds, and then the speculation starts on potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, which the SNB won't like," said Zurich-based Siegenthaler.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cited the risk of deflation as the main reason for trying to check the franc's relentless rise to all-time highs versus the euro, though it conceded at its quarterly June policy meeting that such risks have now lapsed.\par \par \uc2 "Before the SNB undertakes any further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I think they will need to issue fresh verbal warnings on deflationary risks developing," said Frankfurt-based Praefcke.\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 UBS\uc2  expects the euro to weaken to around 1.28 francs in the near term, the bank also forecasts that Swiss policy makers will lift interest rates when they meet Sept. 16. "We're out on a limb on this rate prediction, and certainly the stronger the franc gets, the less likelihood there is of a rate increase," Siegenthaler said.\par \par \uc2 Hildebrand reiterated that the SNB expects full-year growth in gross domestic product of 2%, though the pace of expansion is set to slow in the second half of the year and in 2011.\par \par \uc2 A poll of financial experts last week showed economic expectations in Switzerland rebounded in August from a one-year low, suggesting a more optimistic outlook for the rest of 2010, according to the ZEW institute and \uc2 Credit Suisse Group\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Most other Swiss economic indicators also reflect robust growth, with the purchasing managers index hitting a record in July and the KOF barometer expected to hold near a four-year high.\par \par \uc2 -By Neil MacLucas, Dow Jones Newswires; +41 43 443 8046; neil.maclucas@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 23, 2010 06:08 ET (10:08 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100823e68n002dv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
