\par\par \b \uc2 Swiss SNB  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Reserves Fall To CHF219.3B At End July\b0\par\par\uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2010\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves declined to 219.3 billion Swiss francs ($208.2 billion) by end July from a downwardly revised CHF224.9 billion at the end of June, according to data released Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The CHF5.6 billion drop signals diminished buying of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the franc's appreciation against the euro.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in recent months to curb the franc's excessive gains against the euro, though it appeared to step back from this policy in June, saying signs of deflation had disappeared.\par \par \uc2 In July, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it expects a hefty CHF4 billion book loss in the first half of the year as the franc's 10% appreciation against the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eroded the value of its euro holdings.\par \par \uc2 At 0708 GMT, the Swiss franc was quoted at 1.3827 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Website: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.snb.ch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.snb.ch}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Neil MacLucas, Dow Jones Newswires; +41 43 443 8046; [ 05-08-10 0719GMT ]\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Adds detail, background, comments) \par  \par    By Neil MacLucas \par    Of DOWN JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves fell for a second month running in July as the franc's recent falls against the euro allowed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to step back from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, analysts said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The SNB's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves slipped to CHF219.3 billion francs ($208.2 billion) by end July from a downwardly revised CHF224.9 billion at the end of June, according to data released Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The CHF5.6 billion drop in reserves seems to confirm the SNB has stopped buying euros in recent weeks, and is using the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent rally against the franc to sell the accumulated euros at a better rate," says Thomas Steinemann, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Vontobel.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Switzerland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  repeatedly in recent months to curb the franc's excessive gains against the euro, though it appeared to step back from this policy in June, saying signs of deflation had disappeared.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In July, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  warned it expects a hefty CHF4 billion book loss in the first half of the year as the franc's 10% appreciation against the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in that period eroded the value of its euro holdings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The franc climbed to an all-time high around CHF1.3073 against the euro early July, but since then the euro has rebounded on renewed risk appetites and amid receding concerns about the euro-region's debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0803 GMT, the franc was at CHF1.3820 against the euro, about 5.5% weaker over the past month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The SNB will be pleased at the recent franc declines, although we must not forget the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought large quantities of euros when it was at 1.40 to 1.50 francs," said Zurich-based Steinemann.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The franc's falls against the euro will bring some respite to the SNB which has been facing the dilemma of balancing a robust economic rebound and the export-denting, inflation-boosting effects of a surging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Switzerland's leading KOF economic indicator held near a four-year high in July, and the Purchasing Managers' Index climbed to a record, recent data releases show. The rate of unemployment is forecast to drop for a sixth straight month in July.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "August started with a bang, with the latest Swiss business sentiment indicator Monday topping the expectations of even the most optimistic forecasters of the Swiss economy," according to UBS AG economist Reto Huenerwadel.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  said an interest-rate increase at the SNB's next policy review in September cannot be ruled out, though most other observers don't expect any tightening until year-end, at the earliest.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Website: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.snb.ch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.snb.ch}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Neil MacLucas, Dow Jones Newswires; +41 43 443 8046; [ 05-08-10 0849GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100805e685000sm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
