\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-SNB faces criticism as  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\uc2  lead to loss\b0\par\par\uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2010\par 08:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Sharp Swiss franc rise resulted in 14 bln Sfr \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  loss\par \par \uc2 * SNB's euro holdings soar to 120.5 bln by end Q2\par \par \uc2 * H1 loss will fuel public debate over SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds data from monthly report)\par \par \uc2 By Katie Reid and Sven Egenter\par \par \uc2 ZURICH, July 21 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  expects to post a first-half loss of around 4 billion Swiss francs due to exchange rate losses stemming from massive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The announcement is likely to fuel criticism of the SNB's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  where media and economists have raised concerns about losses on the large amounts of euros the SNB has acquired and the effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The SNB's monthly report for July showed that SNB's euro holdings more than doubled to 120.5 billion euros in the second quarter, taking the euro's share in the SNB's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to 70.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 The overall \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have risen more than five-fold since the SNB launched its policy of fighting a rise in the franc in March 2009, hitting 226.7 billion francs at the end of June.\par \par \uc2 The SNB decided already in December to increase its provisions in order to take potential losses into account.\par \par \uc2 The SNB was applauded for its swift and drastic measures to mitigate the financial crisis, helping the Swiss economy to recover much faster than many other European countries.\par \par \uc2 But public criticism rose after it stepped up its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the euro zone debt crisis before dropping its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pledge in June, saying deflation risks had largely disappeared.\par \par \uc2 EX-CENTRAL BANKERS CRITICISE\par \par \uc2 Switzerland's major broadsheet newspapers have run stories highlighting the risks of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Former SNB chief economist Kurt Schiltknecht told one newspaper \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  had proven to be pointless in the past.\par \par \uc2 "That was a big mistake from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Schiltknecht, who worked for the SNB until 1984, was quoted as saying by Swiss financial newspaper Handelszeitung.\par \par \uc2 Another former SNB chief economist, Georg Rich, said he had agreed with the SNB's policy until this spring. "I started to feel uneasy in May when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought such large amounts of euros," Rich, who left the SNB at the end of 2001, was quoted by Handelszeitung.\par \par \uc2 The franc appreciated more than 10 percent against the euro between early January and the end of June and hit a record high in early July at around 1.3070 per euro<EURCHF=>. Since then, the franc has eased to around 1.36.\par \par \uc2 Losses on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves amounted to over 14 billion francs in the first half of the year, the SNB said.\par \par \uc2 "The income from foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Swiss franc positions and the steep rise in the price of gold limited the extent of the SNB's half-yearly loss, which is expected to reach approximately 4 billion Swiss francs," the SNB.\par \par \uc2 While the public debate has been on potential losses from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must also ensure that the franc liquidity created by the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  is drained quickly enough to avoid a build-up of inflation risks.\par \par \uc2 The SNB increased the issuance and the range of maturities of its own debt -- the so called SNB bills -- and launched reverse repo \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to drain liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The SNB monthly report showed that the amount of outstanding debt certificates had risen to 73.3 billion francs by the end of June from 55 billion at the end of May.\par \par \uc2 The SNB is due to post its first-half results on August 13.\par \par \uc2 The bank said results from the stabilisation fund with toxic assets the SNB bought from \uc2 UBS\uc2  as part of the government bailout for the bank were not yet included in this first-half figure, but they were expected to make a significant positive contribution.\par \par \uc2 For details on the SNB's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves click:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.snb.ch/ext/stats/statmon/pdf/deen/A3_2_Devisenanlagen_der_SNB.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.snb.ch/ext/stats/statmon/pdf/deen/A3_2_Devisenanlagen_der_SNB.pdf}}}\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 SWISS-SNB/RESULTS (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100721e67l000bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
