\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-SNB seen sticking to  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\uc2  at policy meeting\b0\par\par\uc2 461 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 2010\par 07:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats story filed late on Tuesday, with no changes)\par \par \uc2 ZURICH, June 15 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  is widely expected to stick to its policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fight too sharp a rise in the Swiss franc at a quarterly policy review on June 17.\par \par \uc2 Here are some key facts about the SNB's current approach and past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 CURRENT STRATEGY\par \par \uc2 * The SNB launched its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March 2009 as part of a set of drastic measures to fight recession and deflation risks.\par \par \uc2 * The SNB relaxed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance in December saying it would fight an excessive appreciation of the franc decisively. It repeated the policy at its March review. Prior to December, it had said it would fight any appreciation.\par \par \uc2 * The franc has risen as much as 9 percent since the December policy meeting, hitting an all-time high against the euro at 1.3731.<EURCHF=>\par \par \uc2 Analysts assume that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has turned to only slowing the franc's rise, seen as a matter of course given the problems in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 SNB Vice-Chairman Thomas Jordan\uc2  was the latest policy maker to repeat the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  message on May 20. Jordan also said there had been no excessive appreciation of the franc so far. [ID:nLDE64J1XQ] [ID:nWEA1715]\par \par \uc2 * SNB board-member \uc2 Jean-Pierre Danthine\uc2  said that there was theoretically no limit to the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The SNB usually declines to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk.\par \par \uc2 * The SNB only confirmed the very first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on March 12, 2009, which sent the franc down by about 4 percent.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Market participants assume the SNB has stepped in and sold francs many times since its December policy review.\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  first opted to drive the franc down via large salvos into the market but has changed its approach on some occasions to buying euros steadily to keep the franc pinned at a given level. The SNB did this in April, locking the euro-franc rate in at around 1.43.\par \par \uc2 * On June 8 the franc quickly plummeted after hitting an all-time high against the euro, with traders citing the SNB's having stepped in. [ID:nWEA5363]\par \par \uc2 * Traders saw larger \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on February 5, April 1 and May 19 this year.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  VOLUMES:\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves posted their sharpest rise on record in May with a 78.8 billion franc jump, reflecting the high \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  volumes.\par \par \uc2 * Overall, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have risen five fold since the beginning of the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March to 232 billion francs at the end of May. [ID:nLDE6570WH]\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Sven Egenter and Catherine Bosley; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 SWISS-SNB/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100619e66g0002n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
