\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ 2nd UPDATE:Swiss Keep Close Watch On Greece;Deflation Danger Ebbs\b0\par\par\uc2 685 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2010\par 15:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Rewrites, adding detail and SNB comments.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Martin Gelnar \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 BERN (Dow Jones)--Switzerland is keeping a close watch on the Greek debt crisis because any problems in the euro zone could thwart its economic recovery, the head of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability in the euro zone is crucial to Switzerland as the region is the country's biggest export market, \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  President \uc2 Philipp Hildebrand\uc2  said at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's annual meeting in Bern.\par \par \uc2 The details of a Greek rescue package are expected this weekend after Athens agreed with the International Monetary Fund and the European Union to take additional austerity measures, worth around EUR23 billion, as a precondition for financial assistance. The IMF-EU aid package could total up to EUR120 billion over the next three years.\par \par \uc2 "It is also key that other European countries begin to tackle their problems, and some of them have done that," he added, responding to questions regarding the possible widening of the Greek debt crisis to countries such as Portugal and Spain.\par \par \uc2 Fears that the Greek crisis could spread were raised after \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  downgraded its sovereign credit ratings for Spain and Portugal, as well as Greece, this week.\par \par \uc2 Should the Swiss franc appreciate sharply in light of the problems in the euro zone, the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to act to lower the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Hildebrand said. "The SNB won't allow such a development to turn into a new deflation hazard for Switzerland. For this reason, it is acting decisively to prevent an excessive appreciation of the Swiss franc," he said.\par \par \uc2 Hildebrand's comments come amid speculation that the SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in recent days to limit the franc's strength against the euro.\par \par \uc2 The SNB rarely confirms any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but its first-quarter \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment data, published last week, showed a 30 billion franc rise in euro holdings--which is evidence of the euro purchases the bank carried out to limit the franc's surge. In 2009, the SNB's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by more than CHF50 billion.\par \par \uc2 Hildebrand also said the risk has receded on UBS AG's (\uc2 UBS\uc2 ) toxic assets held in StabFund, the SNB-run vehicle, to below $24 billion at the end of 2009.\par \par \uc2 On monetary policy, he said the danger of deflation in \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 --which prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to start \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets a year ago to limit the Swiss franc's appreciation--has receded as the economy's rebound continues.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains generous and continues to supply banks with ample liquidity, although movements in the Swiss franc against the euro over the past few months have caused monetary conditions to tighten somewhat, according to Hildebrand.\par \par \uc2 He said the bank has sufficient leeway to stick with its expansionary monetary policy for the time being, but cautioned that this can't be maintained indefinitely.\par \par \uc2 While the absorption of excess liquidity in the market won't pose a problem technically, the timing of any return to a more normal monetary policy stance will be a challenge, the SNB president said.\par \par \uc2 He stressed that the inflation outlook is still the bank's main guiding principle, but added that the SNB doesn't react "mechanically" to such forecasts. "Aspects such as uncertainty about economic developments and the situation on the financial markets are also factored into the monetary policy decision," he said.\par \par \uc2 The SNB expects average annual inflation of 0.7% for 2010, 0.9% for next year, and 2.2% in 2012. It will publish updated forecasts in mid-June.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  slashed interest rates to a record-low of 0.25% in March 2009. Some observers say it could begin raising rates again in the second half of this year.\par \par \uc2 SNB Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.snb.ch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.snb.ch}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Martin Gelnar, Dow Jones Newswires; +41 43 443 8042; martin.gelnar@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 30, 2010 09:01 ET (13:01 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100430e64u003ou\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
